DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Ipswich (L 2–6)
LOCATION:Ipswich High School
DESCRIPTION:Non-league\nFinal: Danvers 2\, Ipswich 6\nIt was 1–1 after on
 e quarter before Ipswich took control in the second. Kyla Moroney had a go
 al and an assist\, and the two Danvers goalkeepers combined for 11 saves.\
 nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/sc
 hedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-6@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Beverly (L 0–2)
LOCATION:Forti Field\, Beverly
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 0\, Beverly 2\nThe Falc
 ons played their rival to a scoreless first half and held Beverly to six c
 orners\, but the unbeaten-in-the-league Panthers scored in the third and f
 ourth quarters. Eva Selaya-Mendez made 11 saves.\nSchedule and results: ht
 tps://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-7@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Bishop Fenwick (T 2–2)
LOCATION:Bishop Fenwick\, Peabody
DESCRIPTION:Non-league\nFinal: Danvers 2\, Bishop Fenwick 2\nZoie Abell bur
 ied a pass from Kyla Moroney off a penalty corner with no time left on the
  clock to earn a tie at one-loss Bishop Fenwick. Moroney scored the first 
 Danvers goal and Eva Selaya-Mendez stopped 11 shots.\nSchedule and results
 : https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-8@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Gloucester (L 2–5)
LOCATION:Newell Stadium\, Gloucester
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 2\, Gloucester 5\nFirst
 -half goals from Zoie Abell and Addie Moore\, both set up by Kyla Moroney\
 , had Danvers level with unbeaten Gloucester at halftime before a tough th
 ird quarter. Eva Selaya-Mendez made a career-high 21 saves.\nSchedule and 
 results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-9@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Swampscott (W 4–2)
LOCATION:Blocksidge Field\, Swampscott
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 4\, Swampscott 2\nDown 
 a goal at halftime\, the Falcons scored three unanswered in the second hal
 f. Olivia Henry and Kyla Moroney each had a goal and an assist\, Addie Moo
 re scored\, and sophomore Elynne Silva got her first varsity goal.\nSchedu
 le and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.
 html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-10@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T173000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey vs Masconomet (L 1–3)
LOCATION:Dr. Deering Stadium\, Danvers
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 1\, Masconomet 3\nKyla 
 Moroney finished a pass from Olivia Henry just 50 seconds in for a 1–0 l
 ead\, but the defending conference champions answered with three. Eva Sela
 ya-Mendez made six saves.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsath
 letics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-11@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T154500
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey vs Gloucester (L 0–5)
LOCATION:Dr. Deering Stadium\, Danvers
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 0\, Gloucester 5\nUnbea
 ten Gloucester\, the conference leader\, kept a clean sheet and clinched a
  state tournament berth. Olivia Henry made plays at both ends\, Rylee Shep
 pard was strong on defense\, and Kyla Moroney was double-teamed for most o
 f the afternoon. Eva Selaya-Mendez made seven saves.\nSchedule and results
 : https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
